  "2026-10-18T05:11:47.743Z",codex-agent,"Deferred orientation scope also includes richer extension discovery policy, nonminimal manifest controls and execution of declared context_relevance service overrides. The core native slice fails closed on these boundaries instead of executing extension code. Future acceptance must cover configured enable/disable policy, version/engine bounds, contribution inventories and scorer activation against the pinned oracle."
  "2026-10-19T12:26:44.135Z",codex-agent,"Scope: native default and deep context sections, relationship packets, producer continuation and output parity against the locked oracle. Preserve projection-based reads from #94. Validate synthetic fixtures and an immutable real tracker copy; publish aggregate timing only. The broader follow-up description remains beyond this bounded task."
  "2026-10-19T12:42:00.295Z",codex-agent,"Implementation in progress: preserve the brief metadata projection; add selected deep-section fields, descendant completion, retained compact activity, files/workload/staleness/test summaries and ranked continuation. Relationship packets use deps --format context, matching the pinned command contract. The immutable real copy contains 1254 items at capture. Initial parity exposed the existing static extension-health refusal for inert manifest metadata; extending that read boundary. Synthetic dependencies retain created_at because the locked oracle has the already tracked timestamp-sort defect."
  "2026-10-19T13:17:21.187Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replace only Workspace::context_with_global with its origin/main implementation, leaving the new regression and all other functions intact. cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib orientation_context::tests::deep_sections_preserve_relationships_and_evidence -- --exact fails behaviorally (0 passed, 1 failed; exit 101) because deep native context is refused. Restore the implementation byte-for-byte: the identical command passes (1 passed, 0 failed; exit 0). Expanded context oracle matrix and bounded relationship packet matrix each pass independently. Preserve the locked oracle quirks: legacy depends_on is ignored by blocker detail resolution; packet token settlement excludes subsequently attached alias counts; infeasible packet roots remain unknown_error refusals. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-19T13:29:17.045Z",codex-agent,"Validation checkpoint: the native deep-section regression passes, its single-function behavioral revert fails, all 30 real-copy comparisons passed with authoritative hashes unchanged, and both expanded context and relationship-packet oracle matrices passed independently. Added conservative extension minimum-version and supported-field validation so the static summary retains explicit boundaries rather than accepting unsupported controls. Preparing a draft PR to run the unchanged cross-platform release gates while final coverage and release-binary measurements continue. The item remains claimed and in progress."
  "2026-10-19T13:34:37.683Z",codex-agent,"Added an independent 201-item oracle regression for the completion rounding boundary: JavaScript computes Math.round(29 / 200 * 100) as 14. Native completion now preserves the IEEE division-and-rounding sequence before producing its integer field. The linked test wrapper accepts an optional integration suite while retaining sanitized compiler/test output. Final release measurements will use the frozen binary after these boundary fixes."
  "2026-10-19T13:38:09.456Z",codex-agent,"The first full instrumented run reached the orientation suite with its preceding suites passing, then exposed an obsolete deferred-option assertion: context --after and packet --cursor/--direction/--kind are now implemented. Updated only that deferral inventory; positive oracle comparisons cover the supported controls. Independent 201-item completion-rounding oracle regression passes. Current strict Clippy passes. Draft PR #97 now carries the implementation; final gate totals and measurements remain pending."
  "2026-10-19T13:38:25.120Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding checkpoint: the draft is PR #98, https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/98. The #97 reference in that checkpoint was incorrect. The implementation branch remains feat/native-context-sections."
  "2026-10-19T13:59:14.815Z",codex-agent,"Additional numeric regression proof: reverting only completion and packet-budget arithmetic to integer shortcuts produced 41 passing and 2 failing orientation unit tests; restoring the implementation produced 43 passing and 0 failing tests. The pinned oracle uses IEEE floating-point evaluation, including 29/200 completion rendering as 14 percent and a 470/846 budget reduction producing 234. Added blocked-fallback deep differentials and explicit packet refusal comparisons; preserving the published raw TypeError text and JSON unknown_error envelope for infeasible packet budgets. No oracle pin or gate threshold changed."
  "2026-10-19T14:05:19.198Z",codex-agent,"All three linked test commands passed: 1 native deep regression, 5 packet unit tests, and 1 independent completion oracle regression. Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the aggregate result without changing that policy. Fresh-clone health with isolated Git identity and required merge drivers passes. Expanded the real-copy harness to compare representative relationship roots, encodings, bounds and continuation in addition to the 30 context comparisons. Added custom activity-limit, retained-history failure propagation and stale-order section coverage; no runtime dependency or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-19T14:14:06.555Z",codex-agent,"Focused branch instrumentation now passes 44 orientation unit tests. The retained-activity iterator boundary was extracted so its original real filesystem error and propagation can be exercised without SDK mocks or timing-dependent directory races. Ordinary exact-head CI passed all 501 tests on Linux and macOS; full instrumented aggregate gates remain pending. Recorded the isolated Windows list-latency ceiling miss on existing performance item pm-rust-wdj4; context itself passed that job. The final real-copy measurement will use the rebuilt production binary, with no mixing of binary hashes."
  "2026-10-19T14:18:39.032Z",codex-agent,"The full Linux aggregate at 921275d ran 501 ordinary and 501 instrumented tests successfully, then correctly rejected coverage: seven missed regions and one missed branch. Added targeted cases for the reported activity limit, stale sorting, history propagation, unknown extension-control branch and invalid packet direction through Workspace::deps. The updated 44-test orientation unit run passes; the unchanged complete coverage gate will be rerun on the next head. All three platforms passed the ordinary 501-test suite. No exclusion, threshold, dependency pin or latency ceiling was changed."
  "2026-10-19T14:40:54.395Z",codex-agent,"Count correction and current-source checkpoint: ordinary CI at 365d805 passed 502 tests on Linux, 498 on macOS and 493 on Windows, each across 20 suites with zero failures or ignored tests. Platform-specific test selections explain the differences; earlier comments using the Linux count for every platform were imprecise. All three unchanged latency jobs passed, including context p95 of 118.27 ms, 126.46 ms and 213.52 ms respectively below the 250 ms ceiling. Full aggregate coverage jobs remain pending. Bun orientation passed all 24 tests on the earlier binary; the same suite is rerunning against the final production source. The real-copy harness timestamp flag is now scoped to context rather than packet reads."
  "2026-10-19T14:51:43.654Z",codex-agent,"The complete instrumented Linux and macOS runs at 365d805 passed their test suites and reached 100 percent functions and branches, but rejected one remaining activity-iterator line/region. Changed the private iterator boundary from generic specialization to one borrowed iterator implementation, so the real filesystem-error test and production reads exercise the same function. Strengthened nested descendant and progress-order fixtures plus original I/O kind/path assertions. The updated stable orientation unit run passes all 44 tests. Rebuilt the optimized binary and restarted final-source Bun acceptance and real-copy comparisons; interrupted runs are not counted as passing final evidence. Coverage thresholds and source scope remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T15:00:07.127Z",codex-agent,"At 63d359e, the 44-test focused instrumented orientation run passes. Both new modules, orientation_context/sections.rs and orientation_deps/packet.rs, now measure 100 percent lines, functions, regions and branches without exclusions or threshold changes. Strict Clippy passes. The frozen optimized binary passed all 26 real-copy relationship comparisons across two representative roots, including TOON/JSON, summary, incoming traversal, node/token limits and three cursor pages per root. The combined real-copy run is now executing its context matrix and will verify authoritative hashes at completion. Whole-crate aggregate gates remain pending on this head."
  "2026-10-19T15:06:13.552Z",codex-agent,"Final-source acceptance and real-copy measurement passed at implementation head 63d359e. Bun ran all 24 orientation differential tests with zero failures or ignored tests. All three linked commands passed again: seven underlying test executions, with evidence recording unchanged at project tracking_disabled policy. The optimized binary passed 56 complete stdout/stderr/status comparisons: 30 context and 26 packet cases across two roots. The captured real tracker had 1254 items rather than the earlier stated 1251; all 2527 authoritative item/history files retained their hashes. Thirty alternating fresh-process samples per runtime/command: default native p50/p95 81.0/291.0 ms versus pinned TS 1402.2/5101.8 ms; deep native 445.7/598.0 ms versus TS 1905.0/2684.5 ms. The clock-pinned driver disables the scheduling-dependent packing guard; the shared-host results are bounded measurements, not a scale guarantee. Aggregate receipt: docs/benchmarks/native-context-sections-2026-10-19.json. Whole-crate CI gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-19T15:24:51.243Z",codex-agent,"Complete unchanged release gates PASSED at 63d359e on all three platforms: Linux 502 ordinary plus 502 instrumented tests, macOS 498 plus 498, Windows 493 plus 493, each across 40 suite executions with zero failures or ignored tests. Every platform measures 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches. Linux exact totals: 13074 lines, 1349 functions, 21821 regions, 3148 branches, all covered. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, required pinned-oracle suites, audit under the existing advisory policy, changelog verification and clone-local merge-driver/strict tracker health checks passed. All nine CI jobs and CodeQL are green. Gate receipt: docs/benchmarks/native-context-gates-2026-10-19.json; run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39273842181. The measured Rust source is frozen; only aggregate receipts, documentation and tracker handoff remain to commit."
