  "2026-10-20T00:21:51.010Z",codex-agent,"Self-review found one more hardcoded Node invocation in the real-copy integration entry point. Both harness entry points now use the same actual typed-module capability probe, honor PM_NODE_INTERPRETER, and distinguish Node --test from Bun test. Fresh current-code revert proofs: restore only harness_behavior to 49265ab -> both opt-in controls fail, exit 101; restore -> 2/2 pass. Restore only real_copy_harness_accepts_matching_packet_refusals to 49265ab -> cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test orientation_differential real_copy_harness_missing_runtime_obeys_opt_in -- --exact --nocapture fails, exit 101; restore -> 1/1 pass. Required Bun harness execution now passes all eight underlying tests. The initial nine linked commands passed 25 underlying executions, but that run preceded the final shared-helper change and is not final-source certification. Rerun all ten linked commands on the frozen source. No SDK mocks, policy changes or production Rust changes. Strict Clippy caught one redundant assertion above the existing function-length bound; removed the duplicate, retaining both staleness controls. The unsupported Bun --test invocation was corrected to Bun test and is excluded from passing evidence."
